    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39947" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaesītus</span></b> ,
			ūs (only in <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>abl. sing.</i>), m.
			quaero. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A seeking</i>, <i>searching</i>
			(postAug.), <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 9, 10, § 51</span></i> (al. quae
			situs).— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Investigation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(rem) semper quaesitu dignam putavi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7, 8, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
